I'm curious if we use bytes comparison if this will be faster, testing shows this is 4-5x faster than str regex, even more if if we return early on presence (instead of parsing the whole body).
```
  _TAG_BYTES_RE = re.compile(rb"\xf3\xa0(?:\x80[\xa0-\xbf]|\x81[\x80-\xbf])")

  def filter(body_bytes: bytes) -> bytes:
      if b"\xf3\xa0\x80" not in body_bytes and b"\xf3\xa0\x81" not in body_bytes:
          return body_bytes
      return _TAG_BYTES_RE.sub(b"", body_bytes)
```
Also, if we can do an early-out, instead of parsing the whole body, we'd gain even more.

